  "note": "SL4-FIN-V4 reference data for the synthetic legal entity GR-TEST: v3 unchanged plus the slice-4 postings (D-SL4-02, D-SL4-10): recovery reserves, CLM recoveries by type (subrogation, salvage, Friendly Settlement) with the counterparty dimension, the BIL cash of receivables (RECEIVABLE_COLLECTED) against the claim recovery clearing, the Friendly Settlement clearing GL-2515 (CLM CLEARING payables and FS recoveries; BIL FS_CLEARING_RELEASED/_CLEARED and FS net receivables settle it), RI recoverables on paid and outstanding separately (GL-1320 / GL-4210, RI-held group UNASSIGNED) and BIL DISBURSEMENT_REVERSED (payment voids; the FIN payment journal itself is reversed by a linked reversal journal, not by a rule). IMMUTABLE once applied by migration 'RecoveryPostings': a change is a new versioned file and a new rule-set version. Accounts GL-1320, GL-2515 and GL-4210 are the illustrative codes of the PRD-09 section 7.1.4 reference chart; GL-1330 (recovery reserve asset), GL-1340 (claim recovery clearing) and GL-4310/4320/4330 (recovery income per type) are PLACEHOLDER codes that are NOT in the PRD-09 chart and NOT the Greek statutory (ELP) chart (OI-FIN-11 open). BIL RECEIVABLE_REGISTERED is a memo entry that FIN does not journalise. The BIL leg shapes of the new entry types are assumptions pinned in Posting/FsBilEntries.cs.",
